ther.\nEach policy must explicitly state complete eligibility, fee/free admission, and deadline/no deadline. No quotas, actual payment collection, queues, IDs, subjective merit, authorization, hidden fields, arithmetic formulas, external data, or arbitrary code. If ANY clause is unsupported, contradictory, ambiguous, missing or not faithfully representable, return rules:null with specific clarification questions in issues. Never partially compile. Executable rules REQUIRE issues:[]; null rules REQUIRE at least one issue. Check negation, age endpoints, nested exceptions, overlapping fee priority, exact time boundaries and complete bilingual meaning before returning. The deterministic checker searches only your structured rules, so their fidelity matters.\n\nExact source snapshot:\n{\"jobId\":\"studio-review-10\",\"drafts\":{\"alice\":\"Mosaic club session. A participant is eligible exactly when their age is at least 16 and at most 80, they are not someone who is none of a resident, a student, and a member, and they are either at least 18 or have guardian consent. The submission instant must be no earlier than 2032-02-29T09:00:00.000Z and earlier than 2032-03-01T09:00:00.000Z; the opening instant is included and the closing instant is excluded. Apply fees only to admitted participants. A scholarship recipient pays nothing. Among people without a scholarship, every student pays $14 USD. Among the remaining people, members with guardian consent pay $9 USD; after that, remaining residents pay $16 USD; anyone still unmatched pays $31 USD. Each person receives only the first applicable price in that order. A scholarship does not waive any admission requirement. No other eligibility conditions or deadlines apply.\"}}"
